{title: 250 - O for a Thousand Tongues to Sing}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #250 • AZMON • 15.13}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: Carl G. Glaser}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 250}
{meta: tune AZMON}
{meta: meter 15.13}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Ofor [G/D]a thousand [F#dim]tongues to [G]sing [F#dim]my [G]great Redeemer's [F#dim]praise,
[D/A]The [Bm]glories [G]of my God [C/G]and King, [G]the [C/G]triumphs [G]of His grace!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]My [G/D]gracious Master [F#dim]and [G]my God,
[D]assist [F#dim]me [G]to proclaim,
[D/A]to [Bm]spread [G]through all [C/G]the [G]earth abroad
[D/A]the [G]honors [C/G]of thy [G]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Jesus! [F#dim]the [G]name that [F#dim]charms [G]our fears,
[D]that [G]bids [F#dim]our [G]sorrows [Am]cease;
[D/A]'tis [Bm]music [G]in [C/G]the [G]sinner's ears,
[D/A]'tis [G]life, and [C/G]health, and [G]peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]He [G/D]breaks [F#dim]the power [G]of canceled sin,
[D]he [G]sets [F#dim]the prisoner [G]free;
[D/A]his [Bm]blood [G]can make [C/G]the [G]foulest clean;
[D/A]his [G]blood availed [C/G]for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]He [G/D]speaks, [F#dim]and listening [G]to his voice,
[D]new [G]life [F#dim]the [G]dead receive;
[D/A]the [Bm]mournful, [G]broken hearts rejoice,
[D/A]the [G]humble [C/G]poor believe.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]Hear [G/D]him, [F#dim]ye [G]deaf; his [F#dim]praise, [G]ye dumb,
[D]your [G]loosened [F#dim]tongues [G]employ;
[D/A]ye [Bm]blind, [G]behold [C/G]your [G]savior come,
[D/A]and [G]leap, ye [C/G]lame, for [G]joy.
{end_of_verse}
